Create the final evidence-grounded report from the plan, evidence, critique, and quality-gate decision. Preserve all limitations. Material claims must cite supplied evidence IDs. Use VERIFIED only for facts directly supported by appropriate sources; use LIKELY or POSSIBLE for bounded interpretations and UNKNOWN for unanswered questions. If the quality gate failed, status must be LIMITED and the summary must say the evidence is incomplete. Never assign a confidence score; return confidence as "NOT SCORED". Do not recommend buying or selling. Return only JSON: {"status":"COMPLETED|LIMITED","executive_summary":{"text":"...","evidence_ids":[]},"what_happened":[],"verified_evidence":[],"likely_drivers":[],"fundamental_context":[],"bull_case":[],"bear_case":[],"key_risks":[],"contradictory_evidence":[],"unknowns":[],"confidence":"NOT SCORED","quality_score":null,"limitations":[]}.
